{"pages": [{"id": 676090, "key": "Type_90_tank", "title": "Type 90 tank", "excerpt": "The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> (<span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span>式戦車, Kyū-maru-shiki-sensha) is a main battle <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> (MBT) of the Japan Ground Self-Defense Force (JGSDF). It was designed and built", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Japanese main battle tank", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 45, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Firing_Type_90_tank.jpg/60px-Firing_Type_90_tank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 1880046, "key": "Type_74_tank", "title": "Type 74 tank", "excerpt": "heavier <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span>, and the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 74 was withdrawn from service in 2024. The JGSDF began studies on new <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> designs with Mitsubishi in 1962, after the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 61", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Main battle tank", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 45, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Tank_type74_ja02.jpg/60px-Tank_type74_ja02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 14207001, "key": "Type_10", "title": "Type 10", "excerpt": "(MBT-X) project, intended to complement and eventually replace the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 74 and <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">tanks</span> in service with the JGSDF. Development began in the 1990s, and", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Japanese main battle tank", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 40, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Type10MBT.jpg/60px-Type10MBT.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 7689143, "key": "Type_61_(tank)", "title": "Type 61 (tank)", "excerpt": "The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 61 <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> (61式戦車, Roku-ichi Shiki sensha) is a main battle <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> developed and used by the Japan Ground Self-Defense Force (JGSDF), built by Mitsubishi", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Main battle tank", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 40, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Museum_of_JGSDF_Camp_Zentsuji_Kagawa_Pref11n.jpg/60px-Museum_of_JGSDF_Camp_Zentsuji_Kagawa_Pref11n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 1694242, "key": "Type_99_tank", "title": "Type 99 tank", "excerpt": "its second generation prototypes, the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span>-II series. The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span>-II was designed by studying the T-72 <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span>. The chassis was to be based on the T-72&#039;s", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "2001 Chinese main battle tank", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 40, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/ZTZ-99A_tank_front_20170902.jpg/60px-ZTZ-99A_tank_front_20170902.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}, {"id": 11082029, "key": "Type_80/88_main_battle_tank", "title": "Type 80/88 main battle tank", "excerpt": "export requirements. Further <span class=\"searchmatch\">tank</span> development commenced which would lead to the <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 80 and <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> <span class=\"searchmatch\">90</span> prototypes. The <span class=\"searchmatch\">Type</span> 80 began development in 1978", "matched_title": null, "anchor": null, "description": "Main battle tank", "thumbnail": {"mimetype": "image/jpeg", "width": 60, "height": 38, "duration": null, "url": "//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Chinese_Type_80-%D0%86%D0%86_Tank.jpg/60px-Chinese_Type_80-%D0%86%D0%86_Tank.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=thumbnail"}}]}